{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e1b9b0f2-6f0e-4a4a-9c2f-echo00000001",
    "name": "Echo API",
    "description": "Postman collection for the Echo messaging API (Next.js App Router).\n\nHOW TO USE:\n1. Set the `baseUrl` collection variable (default: http://localhost:3000).\n2. Run `Auth > Login` first. The session cookie (`echo_session`) is stored automatically by Postman's cookie jar and used by all dashboard endpoints.\n3. Set `projectId`, `templateId`, and `apiKeyId` from the create requests (or copy them from the responses).\n4. For the public send endpoint, set the `apiKey` variable to an API key created via `API Keys > Create API Key`. It is sent as `Authorization: Bearer <apiKey>`.\n\nRESPONSE FORMAT:\nSuccess: { \"success\": true, \"data\": ... }\nError:   { \"success\": false, \"message\": \"...\" }",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": "echo_your_api_key_here",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "projectId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
